Tere paas ek .NET Web API hai.

Tu Azure Portal mein Web App create karta hai.

Wahan do deployment options samajh:

**Azure App Service – Deployment options**

**Option 1: Code**

Direct application deployment

Tu published .NET application files deploy kar sakta hai.

**Option 2: Container**

Docker image deployment

Tu apni custom Docker image deploy kar sakta hai.

Important: App Service ka matlab ye nahi ki Docker use nahi kar sakte. Docker image bhi deploy kar sakte ho.

## **6. App Service Plan kya karta hai?**

Ye concept already discuss kiya tha, lekin article ke context mein samajh.

App Service Plan underlying compute capacity provide karta hai.

Uske andar multiple Web Apps ho sakte hain.

Example:

```
App Service Plan
│
├── ProductService Web App
├── OrderService Web App
└── UserService Web App
```

App Service Plan ke resources aur instances ko Web Apps share kar sakte hain.

Article mein App Service ke underlying worker VMs aur Linux/Windows hosting ka explanation diya gaya hai. Linux code-based hosting mein Microsoft-maintained runtime container images use ho sakti hain; ye tere custom Docker image deployment se alag hai.&#x20;

