# **Part 5: Ab dono ka actual difference samajh**

Bhai, ab tak jo concepts padhe, unko combine karte hain.

**Azure App Service**

**App Service Plan**

**Product Web App**

.NET code or custom Docker image

**Order Web App**

.NET code or custom Docker image

**User Web App**

.NET code or custom Docker image

**Azure Container Apps**

**Container Apps Environment**

**Product Container App** → Replicas\
**Order Container App** → Replicas\
**User Container App** → Replicas

| Feature              | App Service                                                                  | Container Apps                      |
| -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| Deployment           | Code or Docker image                                                         | Container image                     |
| Multiple APIs        | Multiple Web Apps                                                            | Multiple Container Apps             |
| Scaling              | Plan-level compute scaling; per-app scaling options exist on supported tiers | Independent replica scaling per app |
| Scale to zero        | No standard scale-to-zero model                                              | Yes, when configured                |
| Revisions            | Deployment slots                                                             | Revisions                           |
| Event-driven scaling | Not its main strength                                                        | Supports KEDA-based scaling         |
| Kubernetes           | Hidden from you                                                              | Used underneath, hidden from you    |

## **7. Tere project ke liye kaunsa?**

Maan le tu ek simple .NET MVC application bana raha hai, jisme normal controllers, views aur database hai.

**App Service** is a straightforward choice.

Lekin tere e-commerce project mein:

- Multiple Dockerized microservices hain.
- RabbitMQ hai.
- Redis hai.
- Services independently scale ho sakti hain.
- Background workers bhi ho sakte hain.

**Container Apps** is a natural option to explore.

AKS tab seekhenge jab tujhe directly Kubernetes cluster, Pods, Deployments, Services, Ingress aur cluster-level control samajhna ho.

